            <ArticleTitle>[Apical hypertrophic cardiomyopathy associated with coronary artery disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>139-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A fifty-nine year old man, known to have hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, presented worsening of angina. Multivessel coronary artery disease was diagnosed, and he underwent myocardial revascularization (mammary and two safenous grafts were implanted) with good evolution and reduction of left atrium dimension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
